course: dictionary
lesson: 4437
title: Handlebars and how to ride safely
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The handlebars are the bar at the front of a bicycle, scooter or motorbike. You hold its handles to steer, and they turn the front wheel. «Use both brakes, the front one gently» tells you that the brakes are on the handlebars too, so your hands must stay on the bar while you ride.
explain: A bike has two handles on one bar, so we say handlebars, with an s. Grip them firmly with both hands. The text warns that «squeezing only the front brake hard can throw you over the handlebars», so a rider who slams the front brake can fly forward.
explain: Handlebars also has a second meaning. A handlebar moustache is a long moustache curled up at the ends, like the shape of a bike's handlebars. Context tells you which meaning is right: if the sentence talks about a bike, a scooter, steering or brakes, it means the bar on the bike.
fact: Handlebars are the bar with handles that you hold to steer a bicycle, scooter or motorbike.
fact: Handlebars turn the front wheel, so they control which way you go.
fact: «Squeezing only the front brake hard can throw you over the handlebars.» Use both brakes, and squeeze the front one gently.
fact: A handlebar moustache is long and curled up at the ends, like handlebars.
fact: Always keep both hands on the handlebars when you ride, and check them before you set off.
exercise: «Use both brakes, the front one gently.» How should you use the front brake? | *Squeeze it gently | Never use it at all | Squeeze it as hard as you can
exercise: What are the handlebars on a bicycle? | *The bar with handles at the front that you hold to steer | The seat you sit on while pedalling | A bell that rings when you pass people | The part that holds the tyres
exercise: «A boy hit a crack, flew over the handlebars and hurt his head.» Why should riders keep a firm grip on the handlebars? | So they can ring the bell with both hands | *So they can steer and stay in control | So the pedals turn more easily | So the bike goes faster
test: Which word means the handles you hold to steer a bike? | Pedal | Mudguard | Saddle | *Handlebars
test: In «a handlebar moustache», what does handlebar describe? | A fast motorbike | A safe helmet | *A long moustache curled up at the ends | A bicycle wheel
exam: Why is it dangerous to squeeze only the front brake hard? | It stops the pedals from turning | It makes the seat move up | It makes the bell ring too loudly | *It can throw you over the handlebars
